! VFL DIVIDE AT THE EDGES OF ITS DATAPATH -- the cases that matter once
! the division is done by an ITERATIVE BOX (bsv/StretchPAU.bsv,
! mkDivBox) rather than by a combinational `/` and `%` inside
! execute().  decks/vfl_divide.strap is the deck about WHAT divide
! means (the offset, the two signs, the CE manual's zero rule); this
! one is about the arithmetic being right at full width and at the
! last quotient bit, which is where a shift-and-subtract loop goes
! wrong and a `/` operator cannot.
!
! THE RULES, all from Reference Manual printed p.70 (quoted in full at
! the head of decks/vfl_divide.strap):
!   "Both dividend and divisor are treated as integers, and only the
!   integral part of the quotient is developed.  The length of the
!   dividend to the left of the offset cannot exceed 96 significant
!   bits, and the divisor cannot exceed 48 significant numeric bits."
!   "Bits 60-63 of RM form a four-bit remainder sign byte with bit 60,
!   the sign bit, SET TO THE ORIGINAL ACCUMULATOR SIGN.  Bits 61-63
!   are set to zero.  Bits 0-59 of RM are replaced by the integer
!   remainder with the LOW-ORDER REMAINDER BIT IN BIT POSITION 59."
!   and of a zero divisor: "THE DIVISION IS NOT ATTEMPTED, and both
!   the accumulator and the remainder register remain unchanged."
!
! So the whole of RM, read as one 64-bit word, is
!       (remainder << 4) | (original accumulator sign << 3)
! and every RM expectation below is that expression worked by hand.
!
! WHAT EACH CHECK ESTABLISHES, AND THE ARITHMETIC BEHIND IT
!   B1,B2  MAXIMUM WIDTH BOTH WAYS, done first so PF is still clean.
!          Dividend 2**96 - 1 (ninety-six one bits), divisor
!          2**48 - 1 (forty-eight).  (2**48 - 1)(2**48 + 1) =
!          2**96 - 1 exactly, so the quotient is 2**48 + 1 =
!          281474976710657 and the remainder is 0: RM = 0.
!          THE QUOTIENT IS ODD ON PURPOSE -- its last bit is the last
!          one the loop develops.
!   B3     and PF is OFF: 96 and 48 significant bits are the limits,
!          not beyond them.
!   C1,C2  A QUOTIENT WIDER THAN A WORD.  2**96 - 1 divided by 1 is
!          2**96 - 1: the low 64 bits read all ones and the 32 above
!          them read 0xFFFFFFFF.  Every one of the 96 quotient bits is
!          a one, so a loop that stops early, or starts late, shows.
!   C3     remainder 0, RM = 0.
!   A1,A2  DIVIDEND SMALLER THAN DIVISOR.  5 by 7 is 0 remainder 5:
!          RM = 5 << 4 = 80.
!   D1,D2  THE LARGEST REMAINDER A 48-BIT DIVISOR CAN LEAVE.
!          2**49 - 3 by 2**48 - 1: twice the divisor is 2**49 - 2,
!          one too many, so the quotient is 1 and the remainder is
!          (2**49 - 3) - (2**48 - 1) = 2**48 - 2, the divisor less
!          one.  RM = (2**48 - 2) << 4 = 4503599627370464.
!   E1,E2  NEGATIVE DIVIDEND, POSITIVE DIVISOR.  -7 by 2: quotient
!          magnitude 3, sign negative, which as a (B,64,8) field is
!          (3 << 8) | 8 = 776.  Remainder 1 carrying the DIVIDEND's
!          sign: RM = (1 << 4) | 8 = 24.
!   E3,E4  POSITIVE DIVIDEND, NEGATIVE DIVISOR.  7 by -2: the same
!          quotient, 776, and the remainder 1 now POSITIVE because
!          the dividend was: RM = 1 << 4 = 16.  E2 and E4 differ in
!          exactly the sign bit, and vfl_divide.strap's T13 is the
!          negative-by-negative case, so the four sign combinations
!          are all checked between the two decks.
!   G1,G2  A ZERO DIVIDEND.  0 by 3 is 0 remainder 0; RM = 0, which
!          also shows RM was REPLACED (it held 16).
!   F1-F3  THE ZERO DIVISOR IS NEVER SENT TO THE BOX.  9 by 0 after
!          RM has been set to 80 again: the accumulator still holds
!          9, RM still holds 80, and ZD is on.
!
! INJECTIONS, MEASURED 2026-11-16, each in a private copy of the tree
! (so the working file was never edited and needs no restore).  The
! lists are the OBSERVED failing checks of this deck's suite entry:
!
!   THE LAST QUOTIENT BIT DROPPED (mkDivBox's response returns
!     `rg_dq & ~1`): 5 fail -- max_width_quotient (2**48, not 2**48+1),
!     q96_low64 (...FE), largest_remainder_quotient (0), and both
!     mixed-sign quotients (520 = 2 with a minus sign).  Exactly the
!     odd quotients; q96_high32 and every remainder still pass, which
!     is the separation wanted.
!   THE REMAINDER NOT RESTORED (divRestoringStep keeps the difference
!     even when it borrowed): 13 fail -- every quotient and remainder
!     check except q96 (a divisor of 1 never borrows), the PF check
!     and the zero-divisor accumulator and ZD checks (no division).
!     zero_divisor_keeps_rm fails too, as a CASCADE: RM was set by the
!     wrong 5/7 just before, and the zero divisor kept that.
!   ONE REDUCTION CLOCK TOO FEW (the box's clock counter loaded with
!     3 rather than 4, so 72 of the 96 steps run): 11 fail, including max_width_pf_off
!     -- the unfinished quotient sits 24 places too high and its
!     deposit overflows -- and the zero-divisor RM cascade again.
!
! THE CYCLES CHECK PASSED UNDER ALL THREE, and the third is the one to
! notice: a box that is a clock faster is still absorbed, because the
! core takes the clocks the box actually took off the E-box budget.
! That is the design of this step (behaviour, not time, is the box's),
! and it means CYCLES here guards the BUDGET, not the box's speed;
! mkCoreDivBoxTb's literal 4 is what guards that, and it failed under
! the third injection with "clocks = 3, want 4" (on the two vectors
! whose truncated answer happened to be right; the other six failed
! the answer check first).
!
! THE CLOCK COUNT IS ASSERTED EXACTLY, and the number was MEASURED ON
! THE MODEL AS IT WAS BEFORE THE BOX EXISTED (the combinational
! divide).  It checks that the box's clocks are absorbed into the
! E-box budget.  It does NOT check the I-box overlap the box can cost:
! every instruction after a divide here is look-ahead class, so
! nothing overlapped in the first place.  The FP decks that DID move
! are tabled in bsv/StretchPAU.bsv's header.
!
! TIMING RE-PINNED 2026-11-16, 1196 -> 2148 clocks, every value check unchanged.
! VFL E-box time now depends on the operation: bsv/StretchTiming.bsv's
! eboxClocks charges each operation the throughput Perf. Char. Vol. 2's
! atlas prints for it (docs/atlas_oracle.md).  VFL `/` is now charged PDF
! 134's figure, 66 + 4 bytes (+44 signed) -- (BU,64,8) 28.81 us = 96 --
! instead of 8 + 2 bytes; rl_exec_resume still takes the box's own clocks
! out of it, so the box is INSIDE that figure, and no DIVIDE BOX OVERRAN
! line is printed.  What is said above about 1196 is the old budget:
! CYCLES here still guards that the box is absorbed, at the new figure.
!
! RE-PINNED 2026-11-17: CYCLES 2148 -> 2156.  Cause, measured:
! the VFL internal-operand wait (StretchTiming vflInternalOperandClocks = 4, 2026-11-17); injection B restores 2148, injection C leaves 2156.

        SLC, (8)2000.0

! -- maximum width: 96 significant bits by 48 ----------------------
START   L(BU,64), ONES64, 32       ! ones in accumulator bits 32-95
        +(BU,64), ONES32, 0        ! and in 0-31: 2**96 - 1
        /(BU,64), MAX48, 0         ! by 2**48 - 1
        ST(BU,64), B1, 0           ! 2**48 + 1
        L(BU,64), $RM, 0
        ST(BU,64), B2, 0           ! 0
        L(BU,1), $IND+.23, 0
        ST(BU,64), B3, 0           ! PF off

! -- a quotient of 96 one bits --------------------------------------
        L(BU,64), ONES64, 32
        +(BU,64), ONES32, 0
        /(BU,64), ONE, 0           ! by 1
        ST(BU,64), C1, 0           ! low 64 bits: all ones
        ST(BU,32), C2+.32, 64      ! the 32 above them
        L(BU,64), $RM, 0
        ST(BU,64), C3, 0           ! 0

! -- dividend smaller than divisor ----------------------------------
        L(BU,64), FIVE, 0
        /(BU,64), SEVEN, 0
        ST(BU,64), A1, 0           ! 0
        L(BU,64), $RM, 0
        ST(BU,64), A2, 0           ! 5 << 4

! -- the largest remainder -------------------------------------------
        L(BU,64), DVD49, 0         ! 2**49 - 3
        /(BU,64), MAX48, 0
        ST(BU,64), D1, 0           ! 1
        L(BU,64), $RM, 0
        ST(BU,64), D2, 0           ! (2**48 - 2) << 4

! -- the remainder takes the dividend's sign ------------------------
        L(B,64,8), NEG7, 0
        /(B,64,8), POS2, 0
        ST(B,64,8), E1, 0          ! -3
        L(BU,64), $RM, 0
        ST(BU,64), E2, 0           ! (1 << 4) | 8

        L(B,64,8), POS7, 0
        /(B,64,8), NEG2, 0
        ST(B,64,8), E3, 0          ! -3
        L(BU,64), $RM, 0
        ST(BU,64), E4, 0           ! 1 << 4

! -- a zero dividend -------------------------------------------------
        L(BU,64), ZERO, 0
        /(BU,64), THREE, 0
        ST(BU,64), G1, 0           ! 0
        L(BU,64), $RM, 0
        ST(BU,64), G2, 0           ! 0

! -- and the zero divisor, which the box never sees -----------------
        L(BU,64), FIVE, 0
        /(BU,64), SEVEN, 0         ! RM = 80 again
        L(BU,64), NINE, 0
        /(BU,64), ZERO, 0
        ST(BU,64), F1, 0           ! still 9
        L(BU,64), $RM, 0
        ST(BU,64), F2, 0           ! still 80
        L(BU,1), $IND+.24, 0
        ST(BU,64), F3, 0           ! ZD

PASS    BEW, $

        SLC, (8)2200.0

ONES64  DD(BU,64,8), (16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
ONES32  DD(BU,64,8), (16)FFFFFFFF
MAX48   DD(BU,64,8), (16)FFFFFFFFFFFF
ONE     DD(BU,64,8), 1
FIVE    DD(BU,64,8), 5
SEVEN   DD(BU,64,8), 7
THREE   DD(BU,64,8), 3
NINE    DD(BU,64,8), 9
ZERO    DD(BU,64,8), 0
DVD49   DD(BU,64,8), (16)1FFFFFFFFFFFD
! A signed field with byte size 8 is (magnitude << 8) | (sign << 3),
! as in decks/vfl_divide.strap.
NEG7    DD(BU,64,8), 1800            ! -(7)
POS7    DD(BU,64,8), 1792            ! +(7)
NEG2    DD(BU,64,8), 520             ! -(2)
POS2    DD(BU,64,8), 512             ! +(2)

B1      DD(BU,64,8), 0
B2      DD(BU,64,8), 0
B3      DD(BU,64,8), 0
C1      DD(BU,64,8), 0
C2      DD(BU,64,8), 0
C3      DD(BU,64,8), 0
A1      DD(BU,64,8), 0
A2      DD(BU,64,8), 0
D1      DD(BU,64,8), 0
D2      DD(BU,64,8), 0
E1      DD(BU,64,8), 0
E2      DD(BU,64,8), 0
E3      DD(BU,64,8), 0
E4      DD(BU,64,8), 0
G1      DD(BU,64,8), 0
G2      DD(BU,64,8), 0
F1      DD(BU,64,8), 0
F2      DD(BU,64,8), 0
F3      DD(BU,64,8), 0

        END, START
